#ROOMS

#99300
"Before an Old Cathedral"
"The cathedral looming to the north is a work of engineering genius.  It is

formed of thousands of huge, grey granite blocks, each stacked with precision

upon the one below in an interlocking pattern.  The colossal archway to the

north contains the entrance hall of this monolithic building.  Above the

archway, several runes are inscribed.  They appear to be the dates of the

building and blessing of the cathedral.  Several enormous steps lead up to the

entrance hall, formed of the same grey marble visible further down the path.

"
""
301465600 0
21 6 0
D0
""
""
0 -1 99301 0 6
D3
""
""
0 -1 11967 0 6
A
""
""
"continue;

"
E
"to_char"
"@WYou walk up the grey marble steps to the entrance of the cathedral.

"
!
3 0 1
-1
S

#99301
"Old Cathedral - Entrance Hall"
"Here, before the great, looming doors of the cathedral, the entrance hall

seems small.  The doors are each formed of single, huge plank of ironwood, and

are a dull silvery colour.  To the east and west, the entrance hall extends,

creating a larger area for people to congregate.  The floor here is of a

mosaic pattern, formed of thousands of small gems and pieces of stone.  South,

large grey marble steps lead downward and away from the hall.

"
""
